# The worker fetches runs assigned to its Clustro connection over Clustro's
# MCP endpoint (list_runs {status: created}), works on them with Scoutro's
# agent API (/scoutro/api/agent/v1, its own agent token, so Scoutro
# authorizes every call against the worker's actions, collections and
# limits) and reports the result with sources (complete_run / fail_run).
#
# It never uses the Scoutro administrator account, never calls YaCy directly
# and gives the language model no tools: page text is untrusted data, and
# search terms the worker sends to Scoutro pass the same authorization as any
# agent request.
#
# Configuration
#   --agent ID / --secret-file PATH   runtime secret written by Agents & Access
#        (DATA/SETTINGS/agent-runtime/<agent>.secret): scoutroToken,
#        clustroBaseUrl, clustroWorkspaceId, clustroConnectionId,
#        clustroAgentKey. SCOUTRO_AGENT_SECRETS_DIR sets the directory.
#   SCOUTRO_AGENT_URL        agent API base, default
#                            http://127.0.0.1:8091/scoutro/api/agent/v1
#                            (the API proxy of the Olares package)
#   SCOUTRO_AGENT_STATE_DIR  journal of runs (default: <secret dir>/<agent>.state)
#   SCOUTRO_DISCOVERY_DIR    discovery state read for stored classifications
#                            (default: <state dir>/discovery; never written)
#   SCOUTRO_LLM_*            language model as for scoutro-discovery; only used
#                            when the agent grant allows the model
#   SCOUTRO_AGENT_POLL       poll interval in seconds (default 15)
#
# Only one worker process may serve a Clustro connection (Clustro has no
# claim/lease for pulled runs).
#
# Exit codes: 0 normal end (--once), 2 configuration error.

